Urs,

Yes, the expr problem you mentioned was fixed in V5.0 of Tru64 UNIX and
patches are available for earlier versions.  The general problem is that
expr strips leading zeroes.

The fix is not turned on by default though.  To turn it on, you need to run
expr with the CMD_ENV environment variable set to "bsd".  The expr(1) man
page has been updated to mention that.

Tom Woodburn
HP

