>I have @home an AlphaServer 1000 with Tru64 4.0G
> I would buy a workstation 500A but i'm not sure, that supports Tru64 5.1 
> (adaptec scsi controller problem i think.)
>
> Any experience about 500A and Tru64 5.1??

If you have the MX5 model (the one without USB connectors) you have
to change following:

Change the Adaptec SCSI adapter to a Qlogic 1020 or 1040 for example.
If you have a Matrox graphics card you have to change it also.
I would buy a Elsa Gloria Synergy (8 MB) or VX1 (32 MB). These cards
are supported on every OS available for Alpha.
If one day you want to run OpenVMS you have to change the IDE CD-ROM
to a SCSI CD-ROM drive in order to install OpenVMS.

In the model with USB connectors (Miata GL) I think you have only
to change the graphics card if you don't have a supported one.

Reinhard




