> -nl '/dev/disk/cdrom0c'  ${ENT}; done,
> but no success so far.
> Experts !!? 
> Thanks.

Tru64 UNIX uses

        getmntinfo(3)
        getfsstat(2)

It does not have getmntent(), nor /etc/mnttab, nor /etc/mtab

Checking the X/Open standards, getmntent() is not part of the standard.  
But then again, the standards tend to only worry about application APIs 
and not management APIs, which is what mount information would be lumped 
under as it would be different for UNIX, Windows, VMS, etc...

                                        Bob Harris


